<%# Tastatur, measured by Tastatur.

    The same one-line snippet a customer pastes, pointed at this instance's own
    site key — no separate build, no second script, and no way for our copy to
    drift from the one we ship. If it ever stops honouring Do Not Track, we find
    out on our own traffic first.

    Rendered from the application layout only, which is deliberately NOT the
    layout the public shared dashboards use: those pages are viewed by a
    customer's own audience, and putting our measurement on somebody else's
    visitors would be exactly the thing this product exists to refuse.

    Absent unless SELF_MEASUREMENT_SITE_TOKEN is set, so a self-hosted install
    and the test suite emit nothing at all. See Tastatur.self_measurement_token. -%>
<% if Tastatur.self_measurement_token %>
  <script defer data-site="<%= Tastatur.self_measurement_token %>"
          src="<%= Tastatur.tracker_url %>"></script>
<% end %>
